{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1611"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge art/architecture","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-art__architecture.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",557],["+"," Gehry liked to name the images behind his forms: the Dancing House in Prague (1996, with Vlado Milunić), nicknamed „Ginger and Fred“, leans like a pair of dancers; the Experience Music Project in Seattle (2000, today the Museum of Pop Culture) was inspired by smashed electric guitars; and the glass „sails“ of the Fondation Louis Vuitton in Paris (2014) recall a fleet of sailing boats."],["=",412]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",537],["+"," Gehry nannte gern die Bilder hinter seinen Formen: Das Tanzende Haus in Prag (1996, mit Vlado Milunić), „Ginger und Fred“ genannt, neigt sich wie ein Tänzerpaar; das Experience Music Project in Seattle (2000, heute Museum of Pop Culture) wurde von zertrümmerten E-Gitarren inspiriert; und die gläsernen „Segel“ der Fondation Louis Vuitton in Paris (2014) erinnern an eine Flotte von Segelbooten."],["=",392]]}]},
